# REGRESSION, 2026-08-04 (M4). Symptom: `extern function sqrt(x: ?) -> f64` in
# the dump — the parameter type came out as the error type. Cause: lowering asked
# the *locals* table for a parameter's type, and an `extern` has no locals: there
# is no body to use them in, so the resolver never makes any. Fix: the checker now
# records every **written** type (`Checked::written_types`) and lowering asks that.
#
# It matters past the dump. M5a writes a C prototype from exactly these types, and
# clang type-checks the call against the real header (§4.19) — a prototype built
# from the error type would either not compile or, worse, compile wrong.
extern function sqrt(x: f64) -> f64

extern function abs(n: int) -> int

function hypotenuse(a: f64, b: f64) -> f64
    return sqrt(a * a + b * b)

function distance(a: int, b: int) -> int
    return abs(a - b)
